Subject: [PATCH 08067/11362] [outer-loop] pre-register the 20-game QAT h2h
 extension before running it

The 13-game head-to-head returned a null (5-2-6, p=0.453). Extending the sample
after a null is a forking-paths hazard, so the design is committed BEFORE the new
cells run: all 7 remaining games that have an offline L1 window (not a chosen
subset), same decisive criterion, both results reported, and a stated stopping
rule -- 20 games is the corpus ceiling, so this is the last extension.

5 of the 6 ties were BOTH-ZERO floor games where neither arm induced anything.
That is why more games is the lever and more trials is not: the sign test is over
games, and floor games are uninformative by construction.
